-- title:
--   Conjugation by a finite idele preserves relative index of orders
-- statement:
--   Fix rationals $a,b$ and work in the rational quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$. Let $\Lambda,\Lambda'$ be $\mathbb{Z}$-submodules of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, each satisfying the project's predicate [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11), that is: containing $1$, closed under multiplication, spanning $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, and finitely generated over $\mathbb{Z}$; assume $\Lambda' \le \Lambda$. Let $g$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b] \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},f}$, where $\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},f}$ is the finite adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$ built from $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$. For a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule $M$, [`Submodule.conjByFiniteIdele M g`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L31) denotes the preimage, under $x \mapsto x \otimes 1$, of the image of the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z \otimes \alpha$ with $z \in M$ and $\alpha$ a finite adele integral at every height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, under the additive map $x \mapsto g x g^{-1}$; informally $\mathbb{H} \cap g\widehat{M}g^{-1}$. The conclusion is the equality of relative indices of the underlying additive subgroups: the index of [`Submodule.conjByFiniteIdele Λ' g`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L31) in [`Submodule.conjByFiniteIdele Λ g`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L31) equals the index of $\Lambda'$ in $\Lambda$.
--
--   This is the statement that conjugating a pair of nested orders of a rational quaternion algebra by a finite idele leaves the additive index unchanged, so that index data attached to an order (for instance the level of an Eichler order presented as an intersection of two maximal orders) transports along idelic conjugation. It is used in the construction of elements of the normalizer attached to prime Hecke data for Eichler orders.
-- source:
